# Applies to every service built with a repo-root context (auth-service, transaction-service,
# messaging-service — all need /proto available to their build/runtime). Each Dockerfile still
# COPYs only the specific paths it needs, but without this file the *entire* repo — including
# every service's real .env, .git history, and build artifacts — would be uploaded to the
# Docker daemon as build context.

.git/
.github/

# Secrets — every service's real .env, never the committed .env.example templates.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# .NET build output
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
*.user

# Node.js
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Go
services/notification-service/notification-service
services/notification-service/*.exe

# Python
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/.venv/
services/ai-service/.pytest_cache/
services/ai-service/.ruff_cache/

# ai-service RAG data: regenerable/large, not needed by any Docker build.
services/ai-service/data/

# Editor/misc
.vscode/
.idea/
